From 528b220345b4b07bbe8a734e385e300fca6211c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quinby Janes <qcj2000@columbia.edu>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:14:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Apply Dr. Rasouly's September content feedback

- Remove all "Supported by the National Kidney Foundation" claims (badges,
  trust list, footer, page description); keep NKF citations and links.
- Rename "Check if testing may help" to "Genetic Risk Check" in the nav,
  footer, /check page and prompt; keep the end-of-page prompt only on
  Discover why.
- Homepage: drop "Hello, and welcome"; headline now asks about knowing
  the cause of kidney disease.
- Getting started: new headline and intro, remove the hero check button,
  restructure "What you'll find" to Learn / Genetic Risk Check / How to get
  tested, remove "Where are you today?", cite prevalence to Groopman 2019,
  Dahl 2023 and Franceschini 2024.
- Split How genetic testing helps into Discover why and Guide care (Fabry,
  PH1/lumasiran, CoQ10 examples); old URL redirects to Discover why.
- New Help your family page (early diagnosis with 27-year figure cited to
  Gross, Ortiz and Fernandez-Fernandez; family planning moved from Your
  rights; living donors) and new Genetic counselors page.
- Rename Kidney donors to Support living donor decisions; rewrite Sharing
  with family; add CPMG, CureGN, NephCure, AKF and NKF trial links; update
  the DNA scope line and add a MedlinePlus DNA link.
- Nav, card and page titles now match for every Learn topic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0175aRCbwbvCDiP9xhejQHa7
